downs, token/cost usage, merge/suppression reasons, and confidence deltas.\n- Need to preserve local-first and no-required-network behavior as the default.\n- Avoid relying on generic LLM summarization; the product must remain evidence- and contradiction-driven.\n- Any changes to docs must avoid confusing reviewers about whether the project is complete or still in progress.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Where is the demo video hosted, and should the repo/README be updated to link it prominently?\n- Which additional seeded scenarios should be added first to cover under-demonstrated investigators (e.g. network policy, node taints/MemoryPressure, Helm release failures)?\n- Should AI evals be added via replayable cassettes in CI, and if so what minimal corpus size is sufficient?\n- What exact observability fields should be added to trace output to make diagnosis, evaluation, and demoing easier?\n- Should stale roadmap/gap content be split into separate completed vs future-work docs, or just re-labeled with a clear historical disclaimer?\n- How should sensitive-data safety be proved end-to-end so reports/prompts demonstrably avoid leaking secret values?\n\nUse this handoff as background context. If it conflicts with the explicit task below or the current repository state, prioritize the explicit task and repo state.\n\nPlan overview:\n{\n  \"goal\": \"Improve evals, observability, and robustness across the Support Bundle Investigator: build a real eval scorecard across all scenarios, add AI replay/cassette evals, expand scenario corpus for newer investigators, enrich trace.json with seed/retrieval/confidence telemetry, add a debug mode with per-finding provenance, add cost/latency/model summaries for AI runs, and add robustness tests for corrupt/partial/oversized bundles, stress/perf benchmarks, and sensitive-data leakage.\",\n  \"totalSteps\": 16,\n  \"stepTitles\": [\n    \"1. Expand eval scorecard: add ghost-service and multi-namespace-retrieval to GOLDEN_EXPECTATIONS\",\n   